; The two right-hand tables STACK IN A CONTAINER rather than sitting at literal
; offsets, and that is a bug fix rather than tidying.
;
; Stock used to end at y=348 and People used to start at y=360. A PanelContainer
; grows to fit its contents, so the moment the resource roster passed about
; twenty-two rows the stockpile table grew straight through the gap and the two
; tables were drawn on top of each other -- legible nonsense, with People's rows
; showing through Stock's.
;
; That is the *fifth* time a literal sized against a roster has failed in this
; HUD. The four before it were row-count literals and were fixed by deriving the
; counts from the rosters; this one was the panel geometry, which nobody had
; thought of as a roster-sized number. A VBoxContainer makes overlap structurally
; impossible: neither panel can grow into the other because the container decides
; where each one starts.
;
; Each table also scrolls, so a roster longer than the window is bounded rather
; than pushing the other table off the bottom of the screen. Which is the same
; failure one axis over.
[node name="Side" type="VBoxContainer" parent="."]
anchor_left = 1.0
anchor_right = 1.0
anchor_bottom = 1.0
offset_left = -262.0
offset_top = 12.0
offset_right = -14.0
offset_bottom = -40.0
grow_horizontal = 0
theme_override_constants/separation = 10

[node name="Stock" type="PanelContainer" parent="Side"]
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_styles/panel = SubResource("StyleBoxFlat_stock")

